A||N||6||merlin||Gas smell while driving||||5||
Z||000000||merlin||08-15-2000||08:34 AM||||I have been unsuccessful at locating the source of a gas smell that I notice while driving my 1987 GT.  I checked the lines under the car, the lines to the pressure regulator, replaced the vapor canister filter, and gas cap to no avail.  I have not seen any gas puddle under the car and the gas smell is undetectable at idle.  I did connect a fuel pressure gauge and noticed that after the pump builds the pressure to 42lbs. when the ignition is first turned on (without the engine running), the pressure will drop to 30lbs. after about 5 minutes.  Should the pressure hold for a longer time period?  Does this mean I have a leak somewhere?  What else could be causing the gas smell while driving?…  Fuel Injector O-Rings?..<P>Thanks for your help.  <BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||08-15-2000||09:45 AM||||I once had the same thing turned out to be a leaky solder connection on the nipples for the rubber hoses on the tank. I dropped the tank and fixed her all up installed the tank and upon trying to start the car found out that I hadn't reconnected the fuel pump wires.RATS||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||08-15-2000||11:01 AM||||Since you said that you notice the smell <I>while</I> you are driving leads me to believe that the smell is being produced while the engine is processing the fuel - I had a problem similar to that too, turned out it was a sticking injector causing the engine to run rich. i seemed to notice it more when going downhill and decelerating and also with the sunroof open. It was further confirmed by the fact of the deposits on the right rear tailpipe. Injector cleaner didn't help either!! -- had to end up changing the injector (of course, the whole engine was changed at that time too) so, now, new engine, new injector - no smell........<P>I am puzzled tho - with a name like "merlin" you can't locate the source???||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||08-15-2000||03:57 PM||||is it wet when you sit in your seat....<P>I had this problem then was informed that I was not supposed to pour gas into the fuel realease switch....hmmmmm makes you think huh||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrfixit58||08-15-2000||04:06 PM||||Formula,<P>When you asked, "is it wet when you sit in your seat?". I thought you were going to tell him to lay off the bean burittos!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> LOL<P>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierocrazy||08-15-2000||10:24 PM||||Do you have any codes? A VACUEM Leak will run rich||||reg||1
Z||000006||WisconsinGT||08-15-2000||10:51 PM||||Merlin, Just a thought. Since I am having a similer problem...I noticed that my muffler has several leaks that causes my engine area to smell like gas. ||||reg||1
